WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Gather approved inputs. An engineer provides the task. Source systems supply approved, versioned material.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Draft a test. The AI uses the approved context to draft a test. It cannot approve its own work.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Check permission first. The permission gate checks who can run which tool, and on which resource.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Check the test works. The test must pass working code and catch a deliberately inserted fault.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Let a person decide. A reviewer checks the results and chooses approve or hold. The AI cannot self-approve.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Keep an audit trail. Save the run, outputs and decision together. Execution logs are also collected along the way.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Improve the next evaluation. Turn reviewed failures into reusable cases to challenge future versions. This does not approve the current run.
